error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2075-undefined.h` cannot be declared `i32`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: C leaves it undefined, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2075-a-header-constant-c-leaves-undefined-is-refused.hero:19:5
     |
  19 |     constant K_DIV: i32  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2075-undefined.h` line 4 reads `#define K_DIV (INT_MIN / -1)`
  note: C leaves this value undefined: a program reading `K_DIV` would read whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines

